+## Failed session setup
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` with the same session and error objects, and rejects the caller with the original error when those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model-response hooks run after the failed setup, and cleanup can release resources acquired before setup failed ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
+`afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, including a partially completed `beforeSession`, rather than proof that setup succeeded or the model ran. Its existing session argument carries no new started flag: deployers must track acquired resources themselves and tolerate absent or partial allocation. This guarantee is the target of #94.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
